.TH SETENV 1 "OShell Built-in Commands"
.SH NAME
setenv \- set or update an environment variable
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B setenv
.I NAME
.I VALUE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B setenv
command creates or updates an environment variable with the specified name and value.
.PP
Environment variables are stored in the format NAME=VALUE and are available to the shell
and its child processes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B NAME
The name of the environment variable to set or update.
.TP
.B VALUE
The value to assign to the environment variable.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B setenv EDITOR vim
Set EDITOR variable to "vim".
.TP
.B setenv MYVAR "hello world"
Set MYVAR variable to "hello world".
.TP
.B setenv PATH "/bin:/usr/bin:/usr/local/bin"
Update PATH variable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 on error.
.SH ERRORS
Prints "An error has occurred" if:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Incorrect number of arguments (must be exactly 2)
.IP \(bu 2
Maximum number of environment variables is exceeded
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unsetenv (1),
.BR env (1),
.BR bash (1)